{"name": "stab-AC-finechain-lat15", "entry": "bootstrap.py", "warm_start": "logs/tdmpc/tdmpc_biped/2026-07-27_19-56-57/model_best.pt", "variant": "walk-biped-tdmpc", "max_env_steps": 3000000, "flags": ["--plant", "baseline", "--varied_commands", "--seed_transitions", "200000", "--pretrain_updates", "10000", "--bc_plan_std", "0.3"], "overrides": {"rewards.track_lin_vel_xy.weight": 4.0, "rewards.track_ang_vel_z.weight": 2.0, "commands.base_velocity.ranges.lin_vel_x": [0.0, 0.5], "commands.base_velocity.ranges.lin_vel_y": [-0.15, 0.15], "commands.base_velocity.ranges.ang_vel_z": [0.0, 0.0]}, "notes": "FINE-GRAINED MANUAL CHAIN stage 2: warm from Z1 (fwd + lat +-0.1, ratio 0.49) and widen lateral a hair to +-0.15. Z1's tiny step held better (0.49) than V's +-0.2 jump (0.40). KEY: does chaining SMALL increments ACCUMULATE (stage-2 holds ~0.5 at wider range) where coarse +-0.2 compounding did NOT (V/W/X re-collapsed)? If ratio holds as range widens, hand-cranked fine curriculum is viable; if it drops back to ~0.4, only the in-run --cmd_curriculum ramp (50k-step increments) is fine enough."}
